{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_2_types_16_ranges_range_types", "label": "Range types", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/postgresql/pages/phase-2-types/16-ranges.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "First-class values with @>, &&, <<, -|-. Half-open [) by default; discrete types canonicalise [1,10] to [1,11). range(x,x) is empty. pg returns the text form '[1,10)'."}, {"id": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_2_types_16_ranges_exclusion_constraint", "label": "Exclusion constraint", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/postgresql/pages/phase-2-types/16-ranges.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EXCLUDE USING gist (room WITH =, during WITH &&) means no two rows share a room and overlapping times. Violations 23P01. Enforced by an index, so concurrent read-then-write cannot both succeed. Needs btree_gist for the scalar equality."}, {"id": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_2_types_16_ranges_multirange", "label": "Multirange", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/postgresql/pages/phase-2-types/16-ranges.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A plain range must be contiguous; [1,5)+[10,15) is 22000. PostgreSQL 14+ multiranges hold disjoint ranges as one value, for availability windows with gaps."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_2_types_16_ranges_exclusion_constraint", "target": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_2_types_16_ranges_range_types", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/postgresql/pages/phase-2-types/16-ranges.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_2_types_16_ranges_multirange", "target": "docs_postgresql_pages_phase_2_types_16_ranges_range_types", 